            {"role": "Shown", "tx": "AC3T5NXnAWQ796wDFGfg4QVtkHhrJNAiVaAShpHB3nnn", "what": "a deposit of 0.003 NEAR by a new lender refused", "row": 566},
            {"role": "Shown", "tx": "5EKouAqzseLiaDNin9jxMyrJvQ6wyio4PcmPNwZoc2Lb", "what": "a deposit of 0.1025 NEAR credited as 0.1 NEAR", "row": 567},
            {"role": "Shown", "tx": "Db7zDeaAsNcDKTarLsHQL7VM5RAqUTjgSM4icvQUzGXA", "what": "a full withdrawal that freed the entry", "row": 568}
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Limits",
      "clauses": [
        {
          "n": "2.1",
          "kind": "limit",
          "text": "The issuer books the payees, and the issuer can approve a held payment to a payee outside the book. That approval is bounded by the card's asset caps, not by the task bound or the payee's daily limit: it charges those two up to their limits and is not refused by them. This has not been done on chain.",
          "status": "in force",
          "refs": [
            { "role": "Enforced", "file": "contracts/airlock-policy/src/roles.rs", "line": 42, "to": 56, "has": "approve refused for the owner", "name": "require_settle_role" },
            { "role": "Enforced", "file": "contracts/airlock-verdict/src/ledger.rs", "line": 97, "to": 114, "has": "pub fn apply_approval", "name": "apply_approval" },
            { "role": "Enforced", "file": "contracts/airlock-policy/src/policy.rs", "line": 478, "has": "pub fn book_set_root", "name": "book_set_root" },
            { "role": "Tested", "file": "contracts/airlock-policy/src/redteam.rs", "line": 519, "has": "fn rt_con_borrower_pays_himself_is_refused", "name": "rt_con_borrower_pays_himself_is_refused" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "2.2",
          "kind": "limit",
          "text": "A booked merchant that colludes with the borrower can keep what it is paid. Nothing in the code prevents this.",
          "status": "in force",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "n": "2.3",
          "kind": "limit",
          "text": "The pool and the card each hold one full-access key on their own accounts, held by the team: a holder can deploy new code to either contract and move that account's balance. The agent account holds a full-access key and a function-call key whose receiver is the card, for the methods submit_batch and expire. The issuer's account holds one full-access key; the issuer is the owner in the state of the pool and of the card, and keeps the powers of limits 2.11 to 2.14 through those contracts' own methods.",
          "status": "in force",
          "refs": [
            { "role": "Shown", "tx": "FAyo8RPPeUU67nTGgKi7kVStb1YtYs2wnFFMn8bV3m1m", "what": "the function-call key added to the agent account, receiver the card" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "2.4",
          "kind": "limit",
          "text": "The fee is charged on what the card kept, so a sweep before the repay lowers it, and a card that returns everything owes no fee.",
          "status": "in force",
          "refs": [
            { "role": "Enforced", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/lib.rs", "line": 1081, "to": 1084, "has": "math::fee_of(outstanding", "name": "repay" },
            { "role": "Tested", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/tests.rs", "line": 708, "has": "fn repay_charges_the_fee_on_what_the_card_kept_and_returns_the_collateral", "name": "repay_charges_the_fee_on_what_the_card_kept_and_returns_the_collateral" },
            { "role": "Tested", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/tests.rs", "line": 740, "has": "fn a_fully_swept_line_owes_nothing", "name": "a_fully_swept_line_owes_nothing" },
            { "role": "Shown", "tx": "N2344KkGfQG5e3L7p6jwDL8bonzcPoT8mvdqFNhvEi8", "what": "a repay of 0.5 NEAR kept plus its 10 percent fee", "row": 379 }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "2.5",
          "kind": "limit",
          "text": "The issuer sets the terms of new lines. The collateral ratio of new lines changes at once in either direction, and open lines keep theirs. Since the pool was upgraded on 10 November 2026, a cut of the Passport base applies at once and a raise waits for the hold, 60 seconds on this pool. A cut does not lower the draw a repay must keep to count toward the score, and the cap counts what one borrower account holds across all its cards.",
          "status": "in force",
          "refs": [
