            { "role": "Measured", "file": "docs/EVIDENCE.md", "line": 390, "has": "`min_hold_ms` 60000", "name": "the pool's hold, read from the chain" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "2.7",
          "kind": "limit",
          "text": "All of this runs on NEAR's test network with test money, and the card's one Base payment ran on Base Sepolia with test ETH the team put on the card's Base address. The issuer, the borrower, the merchant and the agent are the team's own accounts, and so are the two lenders of the recorded run; the merchant's Base address is derived from the merchant's account.",
          "status": "in force",
          "network": true,
          "refs": [
            { "role": "Measured", "file": "docs/EVIDENCE.md", "line": 350, "has": "between our own accounts", "name": "the accounts of the run" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "2.8",
          "kind": "limit",
          "text": "The pool's terms rest on tests, not proofs. The Lean theorems and the Kani harnesses cover the payment gate of the card, the verdict function, and not the credit pool: terms 1.7 to 1.12 and limits 2.4 to 2.6 and 2.10 to 2.14 cite tests.",
          "status": "in force",
          "refs": [
            { "role": "Tested", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/tests.rs", "line": 1316, "has": "fn property_random_operations_keep_the_accounting", "name": "the pool's property test" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "2.9",
          "kind": "limit",
          "text": "An hourly loop borrows 0.09 NEAR from the pool, pays the booked merchant and repays with a 10 percent fee. Its borrower and merchant are the team's accounts, so the fee the lenders earn from it is the team's own money.",
          "status": "in force",
          "refs": [
            { "role": "Enforced", "file": "runtime/src/economy/facts.ts", "line": 1, "to": 3, "has": "the fee comes from the team's money", "name": "the loop's accounts" },
            { "role": "Enforced", "file": "runtime/src/economy/facts.ts", "line": 24, "to": 26, "has": "LOOP_FEE_BPS = 1000", "name": "0.09 NEAR at 10 percent" },
            { "role": "Shown", "tx": "C3ZKyFdahsiHExAertB1XSubq3LLcQQuEG9xJvKvfwpJ", "what": "the loop's repay with its fee" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "2.10",
          "kind": "limit",
          "text": "Anyone who pays the pool 0.01 NEAR can have it ask the MPC signer it names whether a Base payment is final and succeeded, and the pool keeps the signed answer. A payment can be checked once Base has finalized it, about 21 minutes after the card's payment was mined. The answer binds the transaction to a block hash and names no payee and no amount. The pool does not check the signature, and no line, limit or share price depends on the answer. Two payments were checked on 10 November 2026: one made by an older account of the team, and one made by the card itself.",
          "status": "in force",
          "refs": [
            { "role": "Enforced", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/lib.rs", "line": 1215, "has": "pub fn check_base_payment", "name": "check_base_payment" },
            { "role": "Enforced", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/lib.rs", "line": 1220, "to": 1224, "has": "fee >= BASE_CHECK_FEE", "name": "the fee of 0.01 NEAR" },
            { "role": "Enforced", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/lib.rs", "line": 1260, "has": "pub fn on_base_check", "name": "on_base_check" },
            { "role": "Tested", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/tests.rs", "line": 2290, "has": "fn base_check_asks_the_configured_signer_with_one_yocto", "name": "base_check_asks_the_configured_signer_with_one_yocto" },
            { "role": "Tested", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/tests.rs", "line": 2338, "has": "fn a_signed_answer_is_recorded_and_the_view_returns_it", "name": "a_signed_answer_is_recorded_and_the_view_returns_it" },
