            {"role": "Tested", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/tests.rs", "line": 430, "has": "fn register_card_checks_the_roles_the_card_answers", "name": "register_card_checks_the_roles_the_card_answers"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "2.12",
          "kind": "limit",
          "text": "The issuer can lend all the money the pool holds idle to borrower accounts it names, with no waiting period: it sets the collateral ratio of new lines to 0, which applies at once, registers one card for each new borrower account (the pool holds 100 cards at most), each account's cap being the Passport base (1 NEAR on this pool), and opens a line on each card, due up to 90 days later. With one card instead, it announces a raise of the base, which applies 60 seconds later on this pool, and opens one line for everything. Lenders can withdraw no more than the pool holds idle, so they wait for those lines to be repaid or to default.",
          "status": "in force",
          "refs": [
            {"role": "Enforced", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/lib.rs", "line": 1163, "to": 1168, "has": "pub fn set_collateral_bps", "name": "set_collateral_bps"},
