            {"role": "Enforced", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/lib.rs", "line": 1092, "has": "self.floor_base / MIN_QUALIFYING_DRAW_DIV", "name": "repay"},
            {"role": "Tested", "file": "contracts/airlock-credit/src/tests.rs", "line": 1707, "has": "fn a_cut_of_the_base_does_not_lower_the_draw_a_repay_needs_to_count", "name": "a_cut_of_the_base_does_not_lower_the_draw_a_repay_needs_to_count"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "n": "2.14",
          "kind": "limit",
          "text": "A loss that is not recovered keeps deposits closed for every lender. Two calls clear it, and both need the issuer's key: write_off on the pool, and sweep on an AIRLOCK card, whose money the pool credits as a recovery. If the issuer's key is lost, no call of either contract clears such a loss and deposits stay closed for good, while withdrawals of idle money go on; as long as the card account keeps its own key, new card code could still return the money.",
          "status": "in force",
